# Safe filenames

When creating, renaming, or suggesting file paths, use names that work on all three OSes.

## Forbidden

- Path separators: `/` `\`
- Windows reserved chars: `< > : " | ? *`
- Control characters (ASCII 0–31) and null bytes
- Trailing `.` or space (Windows strips these; git and sync tools get confused)
- Leading/trailing spaces anywhere in the name

## Windows reserved basenames (case-insensitive)

Do not use these as the full stem or as a stem followed only by an extension:

`CON`, `PRN`, `AUX`, `NUL`, `COM1`–`COM9`, `LPT1`–`LPT9`

Bad: `con.md`, `COM1.json`. Good: `connection.md`, `com-port-1.json`.

## Defaults for this repo

- Lowercase kebab-case: `my-note-title.md`, not `My Note Title.md`
- ASCII letters, digits, hyphens, underscores, and a single `.` before the extension
- One extension only; no `file..md` or `archive.tar.gz` unless the tool explicitly requires it
- Keep each path component ≤ 200 characters (under the 255-byte filesystem limit with room for paths)
- Prefer NFC Unicode when non-ASCII is required; avoid emoji and combining characters in filenames

## Before writing a file

If the user supplied a title or slug, normalize it:

1. Lowercase
2. Replace spaces and `_` with `-`
3. Strip forbidden characters
4. Collapse repeated hyphens; trim leading/trailing `-`
5. Reject or rename if the result is empty or a reserved Windows name

## Examples

| Bad | Good |
|-----|------|
| `What is RSS?.md` | `what-is-rss.md` |
| `notes/final version.md` | `notes/final-version.md` |
| `report:2026.md` | `report-2026.md` |
| `CON.md` | `connection.md` |
| `post .md` | `post.md` |

When renaming existing files, grep for references (wikilinks, imports, Hugo `slug` aliases) and update them in the same change.
